<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Breda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Breda is a city in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-brabant">North Brabant</a> in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. From 1403 it belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-nassau">House of Nassau</a>, the family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-silent">William the Silent</a>, and its castle was a seat of the princes of Orange. A key fortress in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>, it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-prince-of-orange">Maurice of Nassau</a> in 1590, recaptured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1625 and won back by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in 1637, and the Treaty of Breda was signed there in 1667.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/breda.jpg" alt="Breda" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M.Minderhoud · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Breda_kasteel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
